---
const stats = [
  { value: '2', body: 'numbers per meal. Calories and protein; everything else is estimated.' },
  { value: '±10%', body: 'of your calorie goal still counts as a day on target.' },
  { value: '0', body: 'accounts, ads or trackers. We never see a thing you log.' },
];
---

<section class="px-3 pt-28 sm:px-4 sm:pt-40">
  <div class="reveal rounded-card bg-surface px-6 py-20 text-center sm:px-12 sm:py-32">
    <p class="eyebrow text-ios-orange">Why it works</p>
    <h2 class="display mx-auto mt-6 max-w-5xl text-[clamp(2.6rem,6.6vw,5.75rem)]">
      Roughly right every day beats perfectly right for a week.
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-xl">
      You don't need to know that dinner was 612 calories. Knowing it was about 600, and that you're landing near
      your goal most days, is what actually moves the needle. Macro is built for being mindful, not meticulous.
    </p>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-16 grid max-w-5xl gap-3 sm:mt-20 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-4">
      {
        stats.map((stat) => (
          <div class="rounded-[2rem] bg-white px-7 py-9 text-left sm:px-8 sm:py-10">
            <p class="display text-6xl sm:text-7xl">{stat.value}</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{stat.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
